# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React + TypeScript project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1) using npm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- `package-lock.json` updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File Modified**: `src/App.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `TooltipProvider` context, after the `BrowserRouter`
  - Component placement ensures Analytics tracks all routes and user interactions

### 3. Implementation Details
- Followed the official Vercel Analytics documentation for React/Vite projects
- Used the framework-specific `@vercel/analytics/react` import as recommended
- Placed the Analytics component at the app root level to ensure proper tracking
- Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

### 4. Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ All 51 existing tests passed
- ✅ Linter ran successfully (no new errors introduced)
- ✅ Lock files properly updated

## Next Steps
To activate analytics in production:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Analytics data will be collected automatically and viewable in the dashboard

## Notes
- The Analytics component is lightweight and only loads tracking scripts in production
- No additional configuration is required unless custom event tracking is needed
- Analytics will work automatically once deployed to Vercel
